    "verdict": "No blocking source defect found in the frozen four-file board UI increment, including the final pending-width regression.",
    "reviewed": [
      "The shared selector is used for table, list and board records; projection retains canonical Page objects and manual membership order. Rendering does not mutate the record or grouping data.",
      "New board headings, labels, fields, options and metadata use createElement/textContent/dataset. Required-property Unassigned is disabled and command preparation rejects null for required grouping.",
      "Card moves use the existing database.record-update command with explicit null for Unassigned. No board drag/reorder control or filtered-subset record.reorder command is introduced.",
      "Grouping edits and card moves retain exact candidates through existing recoverable edits. Failed saves leave confirmed canonical pages/views untouched. Retry and discard preserve page bodies, IDs, unknown payloads and unrelated properties. Successful filtered disappearance restores focus to the board and reports saved removal from the visible projection.",
      "View selection uses awaited persistBlockView with a cloned UI candidate, canonical-operation ownership and temporary readonly/disabled editor controls. A failed selection retains the durable prior selection; creating a canonical view followed by selection failure truthfully leaves that view available rather than recreating or rolling it back.",
      "The ordinary click path refuses pending width edits before createDatabaseView; the added same-task input/click regression confirms refusal, then Retry and subsequent creation copying confirmed settings through reload. No stale-reference production fix was needed.",
      "Unsupported subgroup/grouping states remain explicit; imported layout/cardPreview/subgroup metadata is preserved. New views copy relevant visible fields, widths, filters and sorts without altering original views.",
      "Actual service browser tests substitute only Tauri transport and execute typed canonical validation, SQLite storage, UI-state persistence and restart. Browser failure tests abort actual IndexedDB transactions after successful put requests.",
      "The existing 500-record display cap is applied globally before lane rendering; membership order is never rewritten. Empty lane counts/state remain available."
    ],
